/-!
# Witnesses for the noncentral J₂ involution centralizer

The sixty indices mark a candidate simple factor among the 240 published
centralizer words. Five-letter permutations were found from its action on
its five Sylow two-subgroups. Four further indices mark a candidate central factor.
These are only finite witnesses: the companion proof checks the multiplication,
parity, disjointness, and product decompositions against the existing ATLAS words.

Adapted, with the original files preserved, from
`CFSG/Quasithin/Chapter16/Section01To02/OtherPreliminaries/
JankoTwoHigmanSims/J2Inner/NoncentralData.lean`. Only intrinsic carrier
mathematics is used here; the chapter hypotheses are not imported.

Source: the retained ATLAS J2G1-p100B0 data and Aschbacher–Smith 16.1.5(8), p.1172.
The original `J2Inner/source/generate.py` at that source path supplies the
unpacked witnesses. The adjacent `source/pack_tables.py` packs their rows as
integers to avoid repeated reduction of nested vectors. Neither script is a
trusted oracle; the companion Lean module checks the group identities.
-/

